{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03112",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.39,
      "end_seconds": 3.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Good afternoon, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.79,
      "end_seconds": 12.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Yes, come in and sit down. What brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 13.73,
      "end_seconds": 19.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.96,
      "text": "Oh, hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.39,
      "end_seconds": 26.82,
      "duration_seconds": 6.43,
      "text": "So, uh, I've been coughing up large amounts of blood, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.43,
      "end_seconds": 30.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 31.63,
      "end_seconds": 35.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "He takes lansoprazole, 30 milligrams, before breakfast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.89,
      "end_seconds": 36.88,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "Hm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 37.4,
      "end_seconds": 49.29,
      "duration_seconds": 11.89,
      "text": "He is on sumatriptan, 50 milligrams, when needed, I give it to him. He is on mirtazapine, at night, I give it to him."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.12,
      "end_seconds": 53.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 54.76,
      "end_seconds": 63.51,
      "duration_seconds": 8.75,
      "text": "15 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box. He takes Foracort inhaler, twice a day for my asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.19,
      "end_seconds": 68.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Alright, how long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.12,
      "end_seconds": 72.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "It's been two days now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.56,
      "end_seconds": 77.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.5,
      "end_seconds": 83.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "It comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.26,
      "end_seconds": 91.97,
      "duration_seconds": 7.71,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 92.07,
      "end_seconds": 97.47,
      "duration_seconds": 5.4,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.28,
      "end_seconds": 105.51,
      "duration_seconds": 6.23,
      "text": "I was getting to that! And breathlessness as well, since last night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.89,
      "end_seconds": 112.98,
      "duration_seconds": 7.09,
      "text": "I follow. Have you been coughing up large amounts of blood at any time before this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.83,
      "end_seconds": 124.98,
      "duration_seconds": 7.15,
      "text": "So, yes, something like this happened last winter, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.69,
      "end_seconds": 142.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Have you had any fever, chest pain or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.79,
      "end_seconds": 155.65,
      "duration_seconds": 11.86,
      "text": "No, no fever, no chest pain, no weight loss. I did have a gurgling chest at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.6,
      "end_seconds": 161.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Any pins and needles or loss of strength anywhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.02,
      "end_seconds": 165.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "No, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.1,
      "end_seconds": 168.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.76,
      "end_seconds": 171.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.08,
      "end_seconds": 173.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.07,
      "end_seconds": 178.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "No, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.12,
      "end_seconds": 183.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.29,
      "end_seconds": 198.75,
      "duration_seconds": 13.46,
      "text": "Sorry, uh, what was I saying, I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.78,
      "end_seconds": 206.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.23,
      "end_seconds": 236.88,
      "duration_seconds": 24.65,
      "text": "Erm, I've had acid reflux for five years now. I, I have migraines. Hmm, um, I have depression. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it. I've had asthma, yes. I took the morning off to come in today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.67,
      "end_seconds": 248.45,
      "duration_seconds": 9.78,
      "text": "Yes, migraines and asthma are known to us, good to have that clear. Are you in work at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 250.28,
      "end_seconds": 254.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.53,
      "end_seconds": 258.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.68,
      "end_seconds": 274.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.44,
      "end_seconds": 295.93,
      "duration_seconds": 10.49,
      "text": "Okay: respiratory rate 21, pressure 121 over 77, pulse is 85 beats a minute. And SpO2 94 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.85,
      "end_seconds": 302.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.27,
      "end_seconds": 307.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Okay, I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.3,
      "end_seconds": 323.03,
      "duration_seconds": 5.73,
      "text": "You are pale, breathing fast and bringing up fresh blood with every cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.53,
      "end_seconds": 330.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.86,
      "end_seconds": 359.86,
      "duration_seconds": 13.0,
      "text": "Let me tell you where I've got to. The most likely explanation is life-threatening haemoptysis. A pulmonary embolus is also on my list. We should do an urgent CT scan for massive haemoptysis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.91,
      "end_seconds": 363.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "Right, understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.44,
      "end_seconds": 368.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Let's book urgent blood tests to look into bleeding."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 369.31,
      "end_seconds": 371.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Mm, um, alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.33,
      "end_seconds": 393.76,
      "duration_seconds": 21.43,
      "text": "Let's use tranexamic acid, 1 gram, now, single dose. That should help with haemoptysis. Lie on the bleeding side and I am calling the emergency team. I think the emergency team should see you too. We'll catch up straight away. So, that's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 395.62,
      "end_seconds": 397.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Thank you, that's helpful."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 399.55,
      "end_seconds": 400.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}